---
import Legend from './Legend.astro';
import Slider from './Slider.astro';
---

<figure class="kf-widget" data-kf-fuse>
  <div class="kf-widget__head">
    <span class="kf-widget__title">Combining two uncertain altitudes</span>
    <Legend items={[{ label: 'What you believed', tone: 'truth', shape: 'dashed' }, { label: 'What the sensor says', tone: 'second' }, { label: 'Combined', tone: 'estimate' }]} />
  </div>
  <div class="kf-plot" id="fuse-plot" data-plot data-label="Two bell curves and the narrower bell curve you get by combining them"></div>
  <div class="kf-controls">
    <Slider id="fuse-prior-mean" name="priorMean" label="Belief" min={970} max={1030} step={0.5} value={992} />
    <Slider id="fuse-prior-sigma" name="priorSigma" label="Belief σ" min={1} max={20} step={0.5} value={8} />
    <Slider id="fuse-z-mean" name="zMean" label="Reading" min={970} max={1030} step={0.5} value={1010} />
    <Slider id="fuse-z-sigma" name="zSigma" label="Reading σ" min={1} max={20} step={0.5} value={5} />
  </div>
  <dl class="kf-stats">
    <div><dt>Kalman gain K</dt><dd data-stat="gain"></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Combined altitude</dt><dd data-stat="mean"></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Combined <span class="kf-greek">σ</span></dt><dd data-stat="sigma"></dd></div>
  </dl>
  <figcaption class="kf-caption">
    The combined bell is always narrower than both of its parents, and it always sits closer to the more certain one. Make the two σ equal and it lands exactly halfway.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
  import { mountFuse } from '../scripts/fuse';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-kf-fuse]').forEach(mountFuse);
</script>
